.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-SUBSCRIBE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-subscribe \- subscribes a target resource to a bucket's object-created events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm subscribe
.BR \-\-source\-ern | \-s
.I BUCKET-ERN
.BR \-\-target\-ern | \-q
.I QUEUE-ERN
[\fB\-\-type\fR|\fB\-t\fR \fITYPE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Subscribes a target resource to a bucket, so a notification message is
sent to the target every time an object is created in the bucket (via
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-directory (1),
or the underlying put-object/complete-upload actions). Only type
.B SQS
is supported for now, so
.B \-\-target\-ern
must be the ERN of an EQS queue; delivery happens asynchronously via an
internal event bus, and results in a new message being created on the
target queue whose body is a JSON object-created notification:
.IR eventType ", " bucketErn ", " key ", " ern ", " size ", " contentType ", "
and
.IR md5Sum .
.PP
Subscribing is idempotent: subscribing the same source/type/target
combination again returns the same subscription, rather than creating a
duplicate.
.PP
Use
.BR euclid-cli-esm-unsubscribe (1)
to remove a subscription.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-source\-ern " " \fIBUCKET-ERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the bucket to subscribe to. Required.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Subscription type. Only
.I SQS
is supported for now. Defaults to
.IR SQS .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-target\-ern " " \fIQUEUE-ERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the delivery target. For type
.IR SQS ,
this must be an EQS queue ERN. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The subscription's ERN, source, type and target are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, the type is
not
.IR SQS ,
.B \-\-source\-ern
is not an ESM bucket ERN,
.B \-\-target\-ern
is not an EQS queue ERN, or the referenced bucket/queue does not exist.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm subscribe \e
    --source-ern ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:uploads \e
    --target-ern ern:eqs:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:upload-events
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-unsubscribe (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-subscriptions (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-create-queue (1)
